From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: drop the HW checksum offload on an offloaded mesh vdev

ath11k grants NETIF_F_HW_CSUM hw-wide in __ath11k_mac_register(), so
ieee80211_if_add() puts it on the mesh netdev too. On the wifili path
the advertisement is honoured: nss_core_send_buffer() raises
H2N_BIT_FLAG_GEN_IP_TRANSPORT_CHECKSUM for a CHECKSUM_PARTIAL skb and
the firmware completes the checksum. The mesh encap node is handed the
same request - nss_wifi_mesh_tx_buf() reaches that same function - and
does not act on it, so a frame the router generates itself leaves with
the pseudo-header sum still in the field.

The advertisement is also what suppresses every software fallback:
skb_csum_hwoffload_help() in the core sees a checksum bit in
netif_skb_features() and declines, and the IS_HW_CSUM_NOT_ENABLED()
guards in ieee80211_tx_skb_fixup() and ieee80211_mesh_xmit_fast() are
false. Captured on both ends of an 802.11s link, every DHCP OFFER and
DNS reply the router sourced towards a peer carried udp.check = the
bare pseudo-header sum; busybox udhcpc discards those without a log
line in d4_recv_raw_packet(), so a peer that re-joins never completes
DHCP again. Forwarded traffic is unaffected - only locally generated
frames are CHECKSUM_PARTIAL.

Clear the feature for a mesh vdev whose data path is the NSS firmware.
SUPPORTS_MESH_NSS_OFFLOAD is set only under
ab->nss.mesh_nss_offload_enabled, so a mesh vdev that still transmits
through wifili or the host path keeps the offload. Clearing before
hw_features is computed keeps it out of ethtool's changeable set as
well, so the broken advertisement cannot be restored by hand.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

diff --git a/net/mac80211/iface.c b/net/mac80211/iface.c
index 6611ecf..3eadea6 100644
--- a/net/mac80211/iface.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/iface.c
@@ -2397,6 +2397,14 @@ int ieee80211_if_add(struct ieee80211_local *local, const char *name,
 		    ieee80211_hw_check(&local->hw, SUPPORTS_TX_ENCAP_OFFLOAD))
 			ndev->features |= NETIF_F_HW_CSUM;
 
+		/*
+		 * Nothing behind the NSS mesh encap node completes a
+		 * CHECKSUM_PARTIAL: the placeholder sum reaches the air.
+		 */
+		if (type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT &&
+		    ieee80211_hw_check(&local->hw, SUPPORTS_MESH_NSS_OFFLOAD))
+			ndev->features &= ~NETIF_F_HW_CSUM;
+
 		ndev->hw_features |= ndev->features &
 					MAC80211_SUPPORTED_FEATURES_TX;
 		sdata->vif.netdev_features = local->hw.netdev_features;
